1010
01:10:56,002 --> 01:10:58,551
Markieren. Markieren.

1011
01:11:18,107 --> 01:11:19,529
(SPEAKING POLISH)

1012
01:11:52,642 --> 01:11:53,842
Nie! Prosze pana, niech pan...

1013
01:11:54,644 --> 01:11:56,066
(HITS PIANO KEYS)

1014
01:12:00,399 --> 01:12:01,776
GIRL: ...nie znajdziemy!

1015
01:12:02,401 --> 01:12:04,119
(MACHINE GUN FIRE)

1016
01:12:04,195 --> 01:12:05,663
(RAPID PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)

1017
01:12:07,114 --> 01:12:09,242
(SHOUTING IN GERMAN)

1018
01:12:12,036 --> 01:12:13,754
(MACHINE GUN FIRE CONTINUES)

1019
01:12:27,260 --> 01:12:31,436
- Was ist das? Ist das Bach?
- Nein, nein. Mozart.

1020
01:12:31,722 --> 01:12:33,190
Mozart?
Ja.

1021
01:12:53,711 --> 01:12:54,833
Das wollen wir heute noch schaffen?

1022
01:12:54,954 --> 01:12:55,955
Nee, schaffen wir nie.

1023
01:13:01,536 --> 01:13:03,634
Nee, schaffen wir nie.

1024
01:13:03,713 --> 01:13:05,886
I wish this fucking night were over.

1025
01:13:05,965 --> 01:13:07,558
(PIANO PLAYING CONTINUES)

1026
01:13:19,186 --> 01:13:20,187
(PIANO PLAYING STOPS)

1027
01:13:44,712 --> 01:13:46,885
(WHISTLE BLOWING)
OFFICER: Appell! Fünferreihen!

1028
01:13:49,091 --> 01:13:50,092
Antreten!

1029
01:13:53,137 --> 01:13:55,265
Halt, alle anstellen!

1030
01:13:58,260 --> 01:14:00,653
Los, los, Fünferreihen!

1031
01:14:01,938 --> 01:14:03,406
Mützen ab!

1032
01:14:05,608 --> 01:14:07,201
Namen verlesen!

1033
01:14:07,526 --> 01:14:11,497
Wer aufgerufen wird, hebt seine
Hand und ein deutliches Jawohl!

1034
01:14:11,572 --> 01:14:13,370
(OFFICER CALLS OUT NAMES)
MAN: Jawohl.

1035
01:14:17,536 --> 01:14:19,538
- Keller, Fanni!
- Jawohl.

1036
01:14:20,873 --> 01:14:24,343
- Adalbert, Hermann!
- Jawohl.

1037
01:14:25,544 --> 01:14:27,217
- Faber, Dorothea!
- Jawohl.

1038
01:14:27,672 --> 01:14:29,720
- Goldstein, Pola!
- Jawohl.

1039
01:14:31,258 --> 01:14:34,102
- Warmberger, Markus!
- Jawohl.

1040
01:14:36,138 --> 01:14:37,811
Edelstein, Max!

1041
01:14:37,890 --> 01:14:40,063
(SOLDIERS CONTINUE SHOUTING NAMES)

1042
01:14:56,867 --> 01:14:58,585
Appell abtreten!

1043
01:14:59,245 --> 01:15:00,246
Do pracy!

1044
01:15:01,497 --> 01:15:03,966
The worst is over. We are workers now.

1045
01:15:05,418 --> 01:15:07,591
(MAN SPEAKING GERMAN ON PA)

1046
01:15:36,449 --> 01:15:38,076
OFFICER: Keine Müdigkeit vorschützen!

1047
01:15:41,245 --> 01:15:43,213
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1048
01:15:43,539 --> 01:15:46,964
Oh, God, Amon.

1049
01:15:48,836 --> 01:15:50,509
(OFFICER SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

1050
01:15:51,547 --> 01:15:53,970
MAN ON LOUDSPEAKER: Sofort in der Baracke zurückmelden!

1051
01:16:11,067 --> 01:16:12,319
(GUNSHOT)

1052
01:16:13,903 --> 01:16:15,576
(MAN SHOUTING IN GERMAN)

1053
01:16:16,822 --> 01:16:18,290
(RELOADING RIFLE)

1054
01:16:20,993 --> 01:16:23,291
(WOMAN SHRIEKING)

1055
01:16:23,746 --> 01:16:25,999
(OFFICER SHOUTING IN GERMAN)

1056
01:16:34,507 --> 01:16:36,760
(BONES CRACK)

1057
01:16:38,344 --> 01:16:41,188
OFFICER: Komm du mal schön her! Komm du schön!

1058
01:16:41,347 --> 01:16:42,815
Na komm! Na komm!

1059
01:16:46,685 --> 01:16:49,905
Amon, you're such a damned fucking child!

1060
01:16:49,980 --> 01:16:52,074
Wakey, wakey.

1061
01:16:55,986 --> 01:16:57,112
(SIGHS)

1062
01:17:01,742 --> 01:17:03,289
WOMAN: Make coffee.

1063
01:17:03,410 --> 01:17:04,957
Make it yourself.

1064
01:17:20,761 --> 01:17:24,430
MAN: The SS will manage certain industries itself inside Plaszow.

1065
01:17:25,224 --> 01:17:27,647
A metalworks, brush factory,

1066
01:17:27,726 --> 01:17:29,899
another for reprocessing Jewish clothing

1067
01:17:29,979 --> 01:17:33,779
from the ghettos for use by
bombed-out families back home.

1068
01:17:33,858 --> 01:17:37,408
But it's private industry like
yours that stands to benefit most

1069
01:17:37,486 --> 01:17:39,614
by moving inside the wire of
Commandant Amon Goeth's camp...

1070
01:17:39,697 --> 01:17:42,325
No, no, no. Sit, sit. Julian, how are you?

1071
01:17:42,408 --> 01:17:43,830
Good to see you, my friend.

1072
01:17:43,909 --> 01:17:45,911
- Oskar Schindler.
- Leo John.

1073
01:17:46,453 --> 01:17:47,454
(WHISPERS)

1074
01:17:49,498 --> 01:17:50,715
(CHUCKLES)

1075
01:17:51,125 --> 01:17:52,251
Franz, good to see you.

1076
01:17:52,376 --> 01:17:53,502
Hello, Oskar. Glad you could join us.

1077
01:17:53,586 --> 01:17:54,633
My pleasure.

1078
01:17:54,674 --> 01:17:56,847
- Julius.
- How are you? You lost weight.

1079
01:17:56,922 --> 01:17:59,926
Only in the shoulders. Please, everybody, sit down.

1080
01:18:01,385 --> 01:18:03,113
How are you doing? Oskar Schindler.

1081
01:18:05,723 --> 01:18:07,270
We started without you.

1082
01:18:07,391 --> 01:18:08,938
Fine. I miss anything good?

1083
01:18:09,768 --> 01:18:12,191
I was explaining to Herr Bosch and Herr Madritsch

1084
01:18:12,271 --> 01:18:15,366
some of the benefits of moving their factories into Plaszow.

1085
01:18:15,441 --> 01:18:17,284
I meant the food.
(CHUCKLES)

1086
01:18:20,279 --> 01:18:22,202
Since your labor is housed on-site,

1087
01:18:22,323 --> 01:18:24,291
it's available to you at all times.

1088
01:18:24,366 --> 01:18:26,540
You can work them all night if you want.

1089
01:18:27,119 --> 01:18:30,238
Your factory policies, whatever they've been in the past,

1090
01:18:30,255 --> 01:18:31,708
they'll continue to be.

1091
01:18:31,790 --> 01:18:33,063
They'll be respected.

1092
01:18:34,001 --> 01:18:36,344
I have to know, where do you get a suit like that?

1093
01:18:36,461 --> 01:18:37,804
What is that? Is that silk?

1094
01:18:38,088 --> 01:18:39,005
Of course.

1095
01:18:40,466 --> 01:18:41,467
Ja.

1096
01:18:42,259 --> 01:18:44,078
It has a nice sheen about it.

1097
01:18:44,553 --> 01:18:45,354
Thank you.

1098
01:18:45,679 --> 01:18:46,426
Very nice.

1099
01:18:46,805 --> 01:18:49,350
I'd say I'd get you one,
but the man who made it is probably dead.

1100
01:18:50,226 --> 01:18:51,078
I don't know.

1101
01:18:53,145 --> 01:18:55,239
SCHINDLER: I go to work the other day.

1102
01:18:56,649 --> 01:18:57,751
Nobody's there.

1103
01:18:58,734 --> 01:19:02,364
Nobody tells me about this. I have to find out. I have to go in.

1104
01:19:03,739 --> 01:19:05,161
Everybody's gone.

1105
01:19:06,116 --> 01:19:07,834
No. (SIGHS)

1106
01:19:09,119 --> 01:19:10,045
No.

1107
01:19:14,041 --> 01:19:16,510
They're not gone. They're here.

1108
01:19:16,585 --> 01:19:17,533
They're mine!

1109
01:19:20,385 --> 01:19:21,933
Every day that goes by, I'm losing money.

1110
01:19:22,007 --> 01:19:23,680
Every worker that is shot costs me money.

1111
01:19:23,759 --> 01:19:25,966
I have to find somebody else. I have to train them.

1112
01:19:25,969 --> 01:19:26,989
We are going to be making so much money

1113
01:19:27,054 --> 01:19:28,522
that none of this is going to matter.

1114
01:19:28,597 --> 01:19:30,025
It's bad business.

1115
01:19:33,269 --> 01:19:34,270
(SNIFFS)

1116
01:19:43,570 --> 01:19:44,438
Thank you.

1117
01:19:45,489 --> 01:19:46,491
Leave the bottle.

1118
01:19:48,909 --> 01:19:50,002
Take that.

1119
01:19:51,537 --> 01:19:52,381
Lena,

1120
01:19:53,524 --> 01:19:54,443
thank you.

1121
01:20:04,216 --> 01:20:07,220
Scherner told me something else about you.

1122
01:20:09,513 --> 01:20:11,766
Yeah? What's that?

1123
01:20:11,849 --> 01:20:16,400
That you know the meaning of the word "gratitude."

1124
01:20:17,354 --> 01:20:20,233
That it's not some vague thing with you

1125
01:20:20,316 --> 01:20:22,819
like it is with others.

1126
01:20:24,069 --> 01:20:26,413
You want to stay where you are.

1127
01:20:27,323 --> 01:20:29,746
You've got things going on the side.

1128
01:20:30,617 --> 01:20:32,585
Things are good.

1129
01:20:32,661 --> 01:20:36,086
You don't want anybody telling you what to do.

1130
01:20:37,124 --> 01:20:41,379
I can understand all that, you know. I know you.

1131
01:20:43,672 --> 01:20:48,678
What you want is your own sub-camp.

1132
01:20:54,475 --> 01:20:56,295
Do you have any idea what is involved?

1133
01:20:56,970 --> 01:20:59,238
The paperwork alone,
and then you've got to build the fucking thing.

1134
01:20:59,313 --> 01:21:01,987
Getting the fucking permits is enough to drive you crazy.

1135
01:21:02,066 --> 01:21:03,192
Then the engineers show up,

1136
01:21:03,275 --> 01:21:06,028
they stand around, they argue about drainage, foundations,

1137
01:21:06,111 --> 01:21:07,829
codes, exact specifications,

1138
01:21:07,905 --> 01:21:09,703
parallel fences four kilometers long,

1139
01:21:09,823 --> 01:21:11,600
1,200 kilograms of barbed wire,

1140
01:21:11,626 --> 01:21:15,045
6,000 kilograms of electrified fences, ceramic insulators,
(CHUCKLING)

1141
01:21:15,120 --> 01:21:16,880
three cubic meters of air space per prisoner.

1142
01:21:16,955 --> 01:21:19,049
I'm telling you, you want to shoot somebody.
I've been through it,

1143
01:21:19,049 --> 01:21:20,717
you know? I know.

1144
01:21:20,793 --> 01:21:23,546
Well, you know. You've been through it. (SPITS)

1145
01:21:26,799 --> 01:21:29,043
You could make things easier for me.

1146
01:21:32,721 --> 01:21:34,344
I'd be grateful.

1147
01:21:38,852 --> 01:21:40,479
SOLDIER: Aus dem Weg da!

1148
01:21:49,154 --> 01:21:50,121
(DOGS BARKING)

1149
01:21:50,197 --> 01:21:52,040
SOLDIER: Weitergehen! Weitergehen!

1150
01:21:52,116 --> 01:21:53,914
(SOLDIER SPEAKING IN POLISH)

1151
01:21:54,827 --> 01:21:56,579
(WHISTLE BLOWING)

1152
01:22:10,175 --> 01:22:11,343
Where's Stern?

1153
01:22:15,681 --> 01:22:19,902
Goldberg and Chilowicz, make sure I see my cut

1154
01:22:19,977 --> 01:22:23,356
from the factory owners in this camp.

1155
01:22:23,439 --> 01:22:26,864
Leaving you to take care of my main account,

1156
01:22:26,942 --> 01:22:29,491
the Schindler account.

1157
01:22:30,362 --> 01:22:34,092
He wants his independence. I gave it to him.

1158
01:22:34,575 --> 01:22:36,498
But independence costs money.

1159
01:22:37,536 --> 01:22:39,289
This, you understand?

1160
01:22:44,901 --> 01:22:45,718
Look at me.

1161
01:22:57,598 --> 01:23:00,068
Don't forget who you are working for now.

1162
01:23:05,939 --> 01:23:07,407
(WOMAN SHRIEKING)

1163
01:23:07,483 --> 01:23:08,985
(ACCORDION MUSIC PLAYING)

1164
01:23:09,485 --> 01:23:10,486
MAN: Jawohl!

1165
01:23:10,903 --> 01:23:13,873
SCHINDLER: Make sure he stays. He's a slippery bastard!

1166
01:23:21,330 --> 01:23:22,502
We need more wine.

1167
01:23:22,623 --> 01:23:23,795
More wine!

1168
01:23:23,874 --> 01:23:26,423
Stand on my friend. Don't let him leave.

1169
01:23:31,798 --> 01:23:34,142
(GUESTS CHATTERING AND LAUGHING)

1170
01:23:37,137 --> 01:23:39,014
(GUESTS SINGING IN GERMAN)

1171
01:23:41,600 --> 01:23:43,147
(TOASTING IN GERMAN)

1172
01:23:43,427 --> 01:23:44,775
Was passiert denn in einem Leben

1173
01:23:44,804 --> 01:23:46,305
Prost! Prost!

1174
01:23:49,983 --> 01:23:51,280
Thank you, Herr Direktor.

1175
01:23:51,401 --> 01:23:52,653
Prost, Herr Direktor!

1176
01:23:57,908 --> 01:23:58,826
What are you doing?

1177
01:23:59,085 --> 01:24:01,037
What? Scratching my head.

1178
01:24:01,620 --> 01:24:04,840
Makes them think we have lice.
Helps make them keep their distance.

1179
01:24:06,291 --> 01:24:07,000
Do you have lice?

1180
01:24:07,001 --> 01:24:08,499
Do you have your notebook?

1181
01:24:08,544 --> 01:24:10,221
The calendar on my desk has the birthdays

1182
01:24:10,246 --> 01:24:12,389
of our SS friends' wives and children.

1183
01:24:12,464 --> 01:24:13,886
Don't forget to send something.

1184
01:24:14,967 --> 01:24:16,435
Record payoffs to the Main Administration

1185
01:24:16,552 --> 01:24:18,290
and Economics Office, the Arm...

1186
01:24:18,295 --> 01:24:19,813
Slowly, Stern, slowly.

1187
01:24:19,888 --> 01:24:24,075
The Armaments Board, Governor General's
Division of the Interior and Chief of Police

1188
01:24:24,075 --> 01:24:25,398
as "fees."

1189
01:24:25,477 --> 01:24:27,650
And make them on the first of each month,

1190
01:24:27,729 --> 01:24:30,232
as opposed to individual payoffs to our SS contacts.

1191
01:24:30,315 --> 01:24:32,238
The list is in the lower drawer of my desk,

1192
01:24:32,317 --> 01:24:34,319
- which you...
- "First of month..."

1193
01:24:35,571 --> 01:24:38,331
SS contacts list, lower drawer of my desk, which you handle

1194
01:24:38,331 --> 01:24:40,284
as cash contributions to legitimate charities

1195
01:24:40,409 --> 01:24:42,628
sent, of course, to each official's office.

1196
01:24:42,703 --> 01:24:45,001
Dealings with our black market contacts

1197
01:24:45,122 --> 01:24:47,420
listed as suppliers in the legitimate ledger

1198
01:24:47,499 --> 01:24:49,342
- are more complicated.
- Forget it.

1199
01:24:49,418 --> 01:24:51,261
- What do you mean, forget it? You can't forget it.
- It gives me a headache.

1200
01:24:51,336 --> 01:24:53,030
It gives me a headache!

1201
01:24:54,339 --> 01:24:56,057
(DOGS BARKING)

1202
01:24:56,800 --> 01:24:57,801
(SIGHS)

1203
01:25:00,512 --> 01:25:02,359
- I couldn't get you out of here.
- I'll be all right.

1204
01:25:03,849 --> 01:25:08,605
Anyway, I'm here almost every week. Wednesdays, usually.

1205
01:25:08,687 --> 01:25:11,406
I'll look in on you, see how you're doing.

1206
01:25:13,692 --> 01:25:14,587
Here,

1207
01:25:15,705 --> 01:25:16,765
put these in your pocket.

1208
01:25:17,362 --> 01:25:18,214
Come on.

1209
01:25:23,519 --> 01:25:25,371
Herr Direktor, don't let things fall apart.

1210
01:25:25,454 --> 01:25:27,206
I've worked too hard.

1211
01:25:36,214 --> 01:25:37,344
Thanks for...

1212
01:25:38,828 --> 01:25:39,844
Good luck.

1213
01:26:01,823 --> 01:26:04,571
Achtung, Mützen ab!

1214
01:26:14,753 --> 01:26:16,300
- Work!
- An die Arbeit!

1215
01:26:31,645 --> 01:26:33,363
What are you making?

1216
01:26:33,438 --> 01:26:34,860
Hinges, sir.

1217
01:26:38,360 --> 01:26:40,283
I've got some workers coming in tomorrow.

1218
01:26:40,362 --> 01:26:42,080
Where the hell they from again?

1219
01:26:42,155 --> 01:26:43,649
Yugoslavia, Herr Kommandant.

1220
01:26:44,224 --> 01:26:45,652
I've got to make room.

1221
01:26:49,121 --> 01:26:50,889
Make me a hinge.

1222
01:26:51,206 --> 01:26:52,208
Yes, sir.

1223
01:26:57,587 --> 01:26:59,715
(GUARDS MUTTERING)

1224
01:27:24,531 --> 01:27:25,854
Keep going, you're doing well.

1225
01:27:35,959 --> 01:27:37,882
Oh, that's very good.

1226
01:27:38,754 --> 01:27:42,475
But I'm a bit confused, and perhaps you can help me.

1227
01:27:42,549 --> 01:27:46,270
What I don't understand is that you've been working

1228
01:27:46,344 --> 01:27:50,190
since I think, what, about 6:00 this morning?

1229
01:27:51,391 --> 01:27:55,612
Yet, such a small pile of hinges.

1230
01:28:03,069 --> 01:28:04,446
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWS)

1231
01:28:14,539 --> 01:28:15,540
(GUN CLICKS)

1232
01:28:25,050 --> 01:28:26,402
(GUN CLICKS) Oh, Christ.

1233
01:28:26,485 --> 01:28:27,577
May I try that, sir?

1234
01:28:28,053 --> 01:28:30,306
Check the angle lever. Maybe it's bent.

1235
01:28:30,388 --> 01:28:33,517
No, no. You wouldn't hear a click if it was the angle lever.

1236
01:28:33,600 --> 01:28:35,853
- Maybe it's the pin. Maybe the pin shaft is greasy.
- Ja, come on.

1237
01:28:35,936 --> 01:28:37,062
What did I just say?

1238
01:28:37,287 --> 01:28:38,113
Here.

1239
01:28:40,649 --> 01:28:41,650
(GUN CLICKS)

1240
01:28:42,317 --> 01:28:43,739
Herr Kommandant.

1241
01:28:43,819 --> 01:28:49,576
I beg to report that my heap of hinges was so unsatisfactory

1242
01:28:49,658 --> 01:28:53,253
because the machines were being recalibrated this morning.

1243
01:28:53,328 --> 01:28:54,329
(GUN CLICKS)

1244
01:28:55,372 --> 01:28:58,251
I was put on to shoveling coal.

1245
01:28:59,125 --> 01:29:02,925
(GUN CLICKING)

1246
01:29:07,342 --> 01:29:08,343
(GRUNTS)

1247
01:29:09,761 --> 01:29:10,762
(YELLS)

1248
01:29:10,846 --> 01:29:11,847
(SOBBING)

1249
01:29:22,190 --> 01:29:23,237
Strange, huh?

1250
01:29:24,609 --> 01:29:25,501
Yeah.

1251
01:29:30,949 --> 01:29:32,042
Thank you, Muek.

1252
01:29:34,452 --> 01:29:37,582
Ah, Lisiek. Don't touch the leather, it's just been oiled.

1253
01:29:38,164 --> 01:29:39,875
- Rottenführer.
- Oh, for me?

1254
01:29:39,875 --> 01:29:41,502
Oh, thank you very much, Herr Direktor.

1255
01:29:41,585 --> 01:29:42,962
STERN: Herr Direktor!

1256
01:29:44,170 --> 01:29:45,797
Herr Direktor!

1257
01:29:48,967 --> 01:29:50,435
Herr Direktor.

1258
01:29:53,305 --> 01:29:54,727
He was making hinges slowly.

1259
01:29:54,806 --> 01:29:57,429
So the man can turn out a hinge in less than a minute.

1260
01:29:57,429 --> 01:29:58,418
Why the long story?

1261
01:29:59,144 --> 01:30:00,145
Hmm?

1262
01:30:26,630 --> 01:30:28,598
(MACHINES WHIRRING)

1263
01:30:28,673 --> 01:30:30,050
Thank you, sir.

1264
01:30:30,175 --> 01:30:31,152
You're welcome.

1265
01:30:35,138 --> 01:30:37,937
Nobody knows who stole the chicken, hmm?

1266
01:30:38,016 --> 01:30:39,108
Tell him about the chicken.

1267
01:30:39,184 --> 01:30:42,688
A man walks around with a chicken
and nobody notices this.

1268
01:30:43,772 --> 01:30:45,065
Save yourselves.

1269
01:30:46,566 --> 01:30:47,864
Tell him about the chicken.

1270
01:31:04,459 --> 01:31:06,053
Still nobody knows.

1271
01:31:09,923 --> 01:31:11,140
(SOBBING)

1272
01:31:18,223 --> 01:31:21,978
It was you. You committed this crime.

1273
01:31:22,060 --> 01:31:22,611
No, sir.

1274
01:31:22,611 --> 01:31:24,037
But you know who, though.

1275
01:31:24,421 --> 01:31:26,064
- Yes.
- Who?

1276
01:31:28,066 --> 01:31:29,034
Him!

1277
01:31:33,947 --> 01:31:35,790
- He's very gifted.
- Yeah, sure.

1278
01:31:35,907 --> 01:31:37,050
Bring him over.

1279
01:31:40,412 --> 01:31:41,167
Sir.

1280
01:31:43,326 --> 01:31:44,201
Thank you.

1281
01:31:50,130 --> 01:31:51,507
Thank you again, Herr Direktor.

1282
01:31:51,631 --> 01:31:53,008
You're welcome again.

1283
01:31:53,091 --> 01:31:55,594
It's an honor to work for such a great company.

1284
01:31:55,677 --> 01:31:56,678
It's great to have you.

1285
01:31:56,761 --> 01:32:00,448
I promise to learn everything there is
to know about enamelware production.

1286
01:32:00,448 --> 01:32:01,065
That's great.

1287
01:32:13,570 --> 01:32:17,416
- Hello? Miss Elsa Krause is here.
- I only need five minutes.

1288
01:32:17,490 --> 01:32:19,293
She wants to speak to the Herr Direktor.

1289
01:32:40,805 --> 01:32:41,648
Yes.

1290
01:32:46,603 --> 01:32:48,031
He won't see you.

1291
01:33:19,344 --> 01:33:20,592
Please, sit down.

1292
01:33:24,766 --> 01:33:26,109
Pernod? Cognac?

1293
01:33:26,226 --> 01:33:27,603
No. No, thank you.

1294
01:33:28,853 --> 01:33:31,527
So, what can I do for you?

1295
01:33:36,736 --> 01:33:39,285
They say that no one dies here.

1296
01:33:39,364 --> 01:33:41,492
They say your factory is a haven.

1297
01:33:44,327 --> 01:33:46,455
They say you are good.

1298
01:33:49,582 --> 01:33:50,799
Who says that?

1299
01:33:51,876 --> 01:33:53,378
Everyone.

1300
01:34:00,468 --> 01:34:03,062
My name is Regina Perlman, not Elsa Krause.

1301
01:34:03,138 --> 01:34:06,563
I've been living in Krakow on false papers
since the ghetto massacre.

1302
01:34:06,641 --> 01:34:08,609
My parents are in Plaszow.

1303
01:34:08,685 --> 01:34:12,986
Their names are Chana and Jakob Perlman.

1304
01:34:13,064 --> 01:34:16,694
They are older people.
They are killing older people now in Plaszow.

1305
01:34:16,776 --> 01:34:18,476
They bury them up in the forest.

1306
01:34:18,497 --> 01:34:19,315
Look,

1307
01:34:21,197 --> 01:34:22,791
I don't have any money.

1308
01:34:23,867 --> 01:34:26,791
I borrowed these clothes.

1309
01:34:29,747 --> 01:34:30,751
I'm begging you.

1310
01:34:31,753 --> 01:34:32,546
Please.

1311
01:34:33,918 --> 01:34:35,265
Please bring them here.

1312
01:34:35,545 --> 01:34:37,139
I don't do that.

1313
01:34:38,214 --> 01:34:41,935
You've been misled. I ask one thing.

1314
01:34:42,010 --> 01:34:43,853
Whether or not the worker has certain skills.

1315
01:34:43,928 --> 01:34:45,396
That's what I ask and that's what I care about.

1316
01:34:45,471 --> 01:34:47,894
My father is an importer, not a metalworker.

1317
01:34:47,974 --> 01:34:51,844
Such activities are illegal. You will not entrap me!
(CONTINUES ARGUING)

1318
01:34:53,062 --> 01:34:56,012
Cry, and I will have you arrested. I swear to God!

1319
01:34:57,192 --> 01:34:58,444
(SOBBING)

1320
01:35:06,326 --> 01:35:08,605
People die. It's a fact of life.

1321
01:35:09,287 --> 01:35:11,039
He wants to kill everybody? Great!

1322
01:35:11,164 --> 01:35:12,962
What am I supposed to do about it?

1323
01:35:13,041 --> 01:35:15,794
Bring everybody over? Is that what you think?

1324
01:35:15,877 --> 01:35:18,721
Send them over to Schindler. Send them all!

1325
01:35:18,796 --> 01:35:21,059
His place is a haven, didn't you know?

1326
01:35:21,059 --> 01:35:24,853
It's not a factory. It's not an enterprise of any kind.

1327
01:35:24,928 --> 01:35:27,772
It's a haven for rabbis and orphans

1328
01:35:27,847 --> 01:35:30,076
and people with no skills whatsoever!

1329
01:35:31,184 --> 01:35:32,185
(SIGHS)

1330
01:35:33,645 --> 01:35:35,989
You think I don't know what you're doing?

1331
01:35:36,064 --> 01:35:39,534
You're so quiet all the time. I know, I know!

1332
01:35:39,609 --> 01:35:41,081
Are you losing money?

1333
01:35:41,202 --> 01:35:42,074
That's not the point!

1334
01:35:42,153 --> 01:35:44,121
- So the point is?
- It's dangerous!

1335
01:35:44,239 --> 01:35:45,707
It's dangerous to me!

1336
01:35:50,536 --> 01:35:54,006
You have to understand. Goeth is under enormous pressure.

1337
01:35:54,082 --> 01:35:56,110
You have to think of it in his situation.

1338
01:35:58,127 --> 01:36:00,046
He's got this whole place to run.

1339
01:36:00,421 --> 01:36:03,265
He's responsible for everything here, all these people.

1340
01:36:03,341 --> 01:36:05,435
He's got a lot of things to worry about.

1341
01:36:06,886 --> 01:36:10,686
And he's got the war which brings out the worst in people.

1342
01:36:10,765 --> 01:36:14,145
Never the good, always the bad. Always the bad.

1343
01:36:16,354 --> 01:36:20,381
But in normal circumstances
he wouldn't be like this. He'd be all right.

1344
01:36:21,259 --> 01:36:24,408
There'd just be the good aspects of him, which...

1345
01:36:24,487 --> 01:36:25,488
(CHUCKLES)

1346
01:36:25,613 --> 01:36:28,332
He's a wonderful crook.

1347
01:36:28,408 --> 01:36:32,709
A man who loves good food,
good wine, the ladies, making money...

1348
01:36:32,787 --> 01:36:33,789
Killing.

1349
01:36:35,415 --> 01:36:37,133
He can't enjoy it.

1350
01:36:38,251 --> 01:36:40,230
Bejski told me the other day,

1351
01:36:40,313 --> 01:36:43,966
somebody escaped from a work detail outside the wire.

1352
01:36:44,549 --> 01:36:48,144
Goeth lined up everybody from the missing man's barracks.

1353
01:36:48,219 --> 01:36:51,974
He shot the man to the left of Bejski,
the man to the right of him.

1354
01:36:52,056 --> 01:36:55,230
He walked down the line shooting
every other man with a pistol.

1355
01:37:01,316 --> 01:37:02,568
Twenty-five.

1356
01:37:07,739 --> 01:37:09,100
What do you want me to do about it?

1357
01:37:09,240 --> 01:37:10,117
Nothing, nothing.

1358
01:37:11,492 --> 01:37:13,011
We're just talking.

1359
01:37:25,923 --> 01:37:27,220
"Perlman."

1360
01:37:29,260 --> 01:37:30,933
Perlman!

1361
01:37:32,096 --> 01:37:33,769
Husband and wife.

1362
01:37:34,057 --> 01:37:37,652
Jakob and Chana Perlman!

1363
01:37:50,782 --> 01:37:52,476
Have Goldberg bring them over.

1364
01:37:55,953 --> 01:37:57,705
SOLDIER: Mützen ab!

1365
01:37:59,999 --> 01:38:01,967
Appell abtreten!

1366
01:38:36,869 --> 01:38:39,167
(GUESTS SINGING DRUNKENLY IN GERMAN)

1367
01:38:49,507 --> 01:38:52,852
I'm sure this will be better than those rags, Lisiek.

1368
01:38:54,095 --> 01:38:57,640
Herr Direktor,I was just helping Lisiek to find something

1369
01:38:57,715 --> 01:39:00,268
to clean the stains from the Herr Kommandant's bathtub.

1370
01:39:00,351 --> 01:39:01,294
Go clean it.

1371
01:39:01,553 --> 01:39:02,796
Pardon me, Herr Direktor.

1372
01:39:04,981 --> 01:39:06,779
(SCHINDLER CHUCKLES)

1373
01:39:07,525 --> 01:39:09,699
You don't have to report to me, Helen.

1374
01:39:10,778 --> 01:39:13,452
You know who I am? Hmm?

1375
01:39:21,581 --> 01:39:23,083
(WHISPERING) I'm Schindler.

1376
01:39:25,293 --> 01:39:27,671
Of course. I have heard, and

1377
01:39:28,921 --> 01:39:30,649
you have been here before.

1378
01:39:33,843 --> 01:39:36,392
Here, why don't you keep this someplace?

1379
01:39:36,762 --> 01:39:38,089
Go on, take it.

1380
01:39:38,514 --> 01:39:40,107
I get extra food here.

1381
01:39:40,183 --> 01:39:42,089
Well, if you don't want to eat it, trade it.

1382
01:39:43,381 --> 01:39:44,957
Or give it to Lisiek.

1383
01:39:47,565 --> 01:39:49,084
Why not build yourself up?

1384
01:39:54,405 --> 01:39:56,155
My first day here,

1385
01:39:57,934 --> 01:40:02,034
he beat me because I threw out the bones from dinner.

1386
01:40:05,625 --> 01:40:10,176
He came down to the basement at midnight, and he...

1387
01:40:10,254 --> 01:40:12,757
He asked me where they were.

1388
01:40:15,593 --> 01:40:19,223
For his dogs, you understand.

1389
01:40:22,308 --> 01:40:26,233
I said to him, I don't know how I say this.

1390
01:40:26,312 --> 01:40:30,067
I never could say it now, I said to him,

1391
01:40:30,149 --> 01:40:32,402
"Why are you beating me?"

1392
01:40:35,988 --> 01:40:39,583
He said, "The reason I beat you now

1393
01:40:39,659 --> 01:40:43,289
is because you ask why I beat you."

1394
01:40:45,331 --> 01:40:47,333
I know your sufferings, Helen.

1395
01:40:50,753 --> 01:40:52,255
It doesn't matter.

1396
01:40:54,882 --> 01:40:56,976
I have accepted them.

1397
01:40:58,094 --> 01:40:59,596
Accepted them?

1398
01:41:01,889 --> 01:41:03,732
One day he will shoot me.

1399
01:41:03,808 --> 01:41:06,687
No, no, no, he won't shoot you.

1400
01:41:06,769 --> 01:41:09,522
I know. I see things.

1401
01:41:10,690 --> 01:41:13,739
We were on the roof on Monday, young Lisiek and I,

1402
01:41:13,818 --> 01:41:17,322
and we saw the Herr Kommandant
come out of the from door

1403
01:41:17,405 --> 01:41:23,253
and down the steps by the patio, right there below us,

1404
01:41:23,327 --> 01:41:28,083
and there on the steps he drew his gun and he

1405
01:41:28,165 --> 01:41:31,009
shot a woman who was passing by.

1406
01:41:32,378 --> 01:41:35,632
A woman carrying a bundle. Through the throat.

1407
01:41:35,715 --> 01:41:39,390
Just a woman on her way somewhere, you know?

1408
01:41:39,468 --> 01:41:43,098
She was no fatter or thinner

1409
01:41:43,180 --> 01:41:45,774
or slower or faster than anyone else,

1410
01:41:45,850 --> 01:41:50,026
and I couldn't guess what had she done.

1411
01:41:54,525 --> 01:41:57,699
The more you see of the Herr Kommandant,

1412
01:41:57,778 --> 01:42:03,376
the more you see there is no set rules that you can live by.

1413
01:42:03,451 --> 01:42:07,773
You can't say to yourself,
"If I follow these rules, I will be safe."

1414
01:42:11,834 --> 01:42:15,339
He won't shoot you because he enjoys you too much.

1415
01:42:16,464 --> 01:42:20,069
He enjoys you so much he won't even let you wear the star.

1416
01:42:20,551 --> 01:42:22,144
He doesn't want anyone else to know

1417
01:42:22,219 --> 01:42:24,938
it's a Jew he's enjoying.

1418
01:42:28,559 --> 01:42:31,487
He shot the woman from the steps

1419
01:42:31,570 --> 01:42:34,991
because she meant nothing to him.

1420
01:42:36,150 --> 01:42:37,823
She was one of a series,

1421
01:42:37,902 --> 01:42:40,576
neither offending or pleasing him.

1422
01:42:44,533 --> 01:42:46,752
But you, Helen.

1423
01:42:51,123 --> 01:42:55,594
It's all right. It's not that kind of a kiss.

1424
01:43:00,675 --> 01:43:01,676
(SOBBING)

1425
01:43:01,759 --> 01:43:02,711
Thank you.

1426
01:43:03,094 --> 01:43:04,095
Shh.

1427
01:43:08,641 --> 01:43:10,018
Here.

1428
01:43:16,107 --> 01:43:17,984
Right. The wine.

1429
01:43:25,616 --> 01:43:28,495
Wonderful party, Amon. Thank you.

1430
01:43:29,995 --> 01:43:30,996
(GROANS)

1431
01:43:37,086 --> 01:43:39,556
Why do you drink that motor oil?

1432
01:43:40,131 --> 01:43:42,705
Hmm? I send you good stuff all the time.

1433
01:43:43,384 --> 01:43:47,184
Your liver's going to explode like a hand grenade.

1434
01:43:47,263 --> 01:43:49,241
You know, I look at you.
(SNIFFS)

1435
01:43:50,182 --> 01:43:52,055
I watch you.

1436
01:43:53,936 --> 01:43:54,937
(SIGHS)

1437
01:43:55,320 --> 01:43:56,363
You're never drunk.

1438
01:43:57,239 --> 01:43:58,532
(SNIFFS) Oh, that's...

1439
01:44:00,443 --> 01:44:02,366
That's real control.

1440
01:44:03,571 --> 01:44:05,224
Control is power.

1441
01:44:06,782 --> 01:44:08,955
That's power.

1442
01:44:12,872 --> 01:44:15,466
SCHINDLER: Is that why they fear us?

1443
01:44:18,252 --> 01:44:21,273
We have the fucking power to kill, that's why they fear us.

1444
01:44:22,047 --> 01:44:25,347
They fear us because we have the power to kill arbitrarily.

1445
01:44:25,926 --> 01:44:27,849
A man commits a crime, he should know better.

1446
01:44:27,928 --> 01:44:30,852
We have him killed, and we feel pretty good about it.

1447
01:44:30,931 --> 01:44:33,901
Or we kill him ourselves and we feel even better.

1448
01:44:36,020 --> 01:44:37,943
That's not power, though.

1449
01:44:39,190 --> 01:44:42,444
That's justice. It's different than power.

1450
01:44:46,197 --> 01:44:50,373
Power is when we have every justification to kill,

1451
01:44:51,702 --> 01:44:52,874
and we don't.

1452
01:44:54,205 --> 01:44:55,878
You think that's power?

1453
01:44:58,876 --> 01:45:01,000
That's what the emperors had.

1454
01:45:01,074 --> 01:45:02,170
A man stole something,

1455
01:45:02,171 --> 01:45:03,673
he's brought in before the emperor,

1456
01:45:03,756 --> 01:45:08,011
he throws himself down on the ground, he begs for mercy.

1457
01:45:08,093 --> 01:45:10,471
He knows he's going to die.

1458
01:45:13,516 --> 01:45:16,986
And the emperor pardons him.

1459
01:45:18,312 --> 01:45:21,441
This worthless man. He lets him go.

1460
01:45:25,110 --> 01:45:26,862
I think you are drunk.

1461
01:45:28,989 --> 01:45:30,707
That's power, Amon.

1462
01:45:32,076 --> 01:45:35,250
That is power.

1463
01:45:43,087 --> 01:45:45,931
Amon the Good.

1464
01:45:48,801 --> 01:45:52,101
I pardon you. (LAUGHS)

1465
01:45:59,228 --> 01:46:00,228
GOETH: What do they want?

1466
01:46:00,271 --> 01:46:03,821
STERN: I don't know, but they're in
my office now reviewing our books.

1467
01:46:03,899 --> 01:46:05,029
As my accountant,

1468
01:46:06,099 --> 01:46:08,029
tell me, should I be alarmed that the auditors

1469
01:46:08,112 --> 01:46:09,739
- are reviewing my books?
- Well...

1470
01:46:09,822 --> 01:46:11,290
Or have you done your job properly?

1471
01:46:11,407 --> 01:46:12,329
You needn't be alarmed.

1472
01:46:12,908 --> 01:46:14,060
I needn't be alarmed.

1473
01:46:14,785 --> 01:46:15,911
(SHOUTS ANGRILY)

1474
01:46:18,539 --> 01:46:20,382
(GASPS) I'm sorry, sir.

1475
01:46:20,457 --> 01:46:21,751
Do you know how much this saddle is worth?

1476
01:46:22,626 --> 01:46:24,028
Do you know how much it costs?

1477
01:46:29,884 --> 01:46:30,806
All right.

1478
01:46:31,385 --> 01:46:32,637
(PANTING)

1479
01:46:33,596 --> 01:46:34,573
All right.

1480
01:46:38,976 --> 01:46:41,149
Stern, what the hell are you doing following me around?

1481
01:46:51,697 --> 01:46:54,166
MAN ON LOUDSPEAKER: Baracken eins, elf

1482
01:46:54,441 --> 01:46:59,247
fünfzehn und zwounddreißig am Appellplatz melden.

1483
01:47:01,874 --> 01:47:03,217
(WHISTLING)

1484
01:47:05,002 --> 01:47:06,379
(BOTH WHISTLING)

1485
01:47:20,601 --> 01:47:22,103
(CHILDREN CHATTERING)

1486
01:47:25,940 --> 01:47:27,362
(WHIMPERING)

1487
01:47:29,234 --> 01:47:30,827
She was smoking on the job.

1488
01:47:34,907 --> 01:47:36,250
Tell her not to do it again.

1489
01:47:36,825 --> 01:47:38,702
(SHOUTING)

1490
01:47:42,331 --> 01:47:44,049
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

1491
01:47:53,175 --> 01:47:54,722
I have to report, sir.

1492
01:47:56,762 --> 01:47:59,641
I've been unable to remove the stains from your bathtub.

1493
01:48:04,395 --> 01:48:06,147
What are you using, Lisiek?

1494
01:48:06,271 --> 01:48:08,069
Soap, Commandant.

1495
01:48:10,317 --> 01:48:12,194
Soap? Not lye?

1496
01:48:22,246 --> 01:48:26,046
Go ahead, go on, leave. Leave, I pardon you.

1497
01:48:48,022 --> 01:48:49,516
I pardon you.

1498
01:49:10,127 --> 01:49:11,128
(GUNSHOT)

1499
01:49:18,802 --> 01:49:19,803
(GUNSHOT)

1500
01:49:21,972 --> 01:49:22,973
(GUNSHOT)

1501
01:50:27,037 --> 01:50:28,664
(SIGHS)

1502
01:50:42,177 --> 01:50:45,807
WOMAN: Although I am not a rabbi, in these circumstances

1503
01:50:45,889 --> 01:50:48,608
I pray to the Almighty that he will forgive me

1504
01:50:48,684 --> 01:50:51,278
if I intone the blessings.

1505
01:50:51,687 --> 01:50:54,861
Baruch atah hashem ehloheinu melech haolam

1506
01:50:54,940 --> 01:50:57,363
Asher tzivanu al haraayot

1507
01:50:57,901 --> 01:51:01,405
V'asar aleinu et haarusot V'hitir lanu et han'suot

1508
01:51:01,572 --> 01:51:03,745
Al y'dei chupah v'kidushin

1509
01:51:05,242 --> 01:51:11,124
WOMAN SINGER IN CLUB: Milosc tak pieknie tlumaczy

1510
01:51:11,415 --> 01:51:16,797
Zdrade i klamstwo i grzech

1511
01:51:19,006 --> 01:51:24,433
Choc bys ja przeklal w rozpaczy

1512
01:51:25,387 --> 01:51:30,393
Ze jest okrutna i zla

1513
01:51:31,268 --> 01:51:36,650
Milosc ci wszystko wybaczy

1514
01:51:38,609 --> 01:51:43,786
Bo milosc moj mily to ja

1515
01:51:44,114 --> 01:51:45,832
So...

1516
01:51:47,409 --> 01:51:50,504
This is where you come to hide from me.

1517
01:51:51,371 --> 01:51:53,169
I came to tell you

1518
