Itzhak Stern.

2016
02:27:13,616 --> 02:27:15,835
Rebeka and Joseph Bau.

2017
02:27:17,120 --> 02:27:19,043
- Rosalia Nussbaum.
- Wilhelm Nussbaum.

2018
02:27:20,123 --> 02:27:21,875
Jakob Levartov.

2019
02:27:22,917 --> 02:27:25,045
- Farber, Rosa.
- Farber, Andrzej.

2020
02:27:25,879 --> 02:27:26,926
Sara.

2021
02:27:27,088 --> 02:27:28,180
Friehof, Fischel.

2022
02:27:29,799 --> 02:27:31,176
Mietek Pemper.

2023
02:27:31,885 --> 02:27:33,808
Poldek and Mila Pfefferberg.

2024
02:27:34,596 --> 02:27:36,644
Horowitz, Dolek.

2025
02:27:38,099 --> 02:27:39,396
Adam Levy.

2026
02:27:40,310 --> 02:27:41,937
Marcel Goldberg.

2027
02:27:42,645 --> 02:27:44,864
Klipstein, Isak David.

2028
02:27:46,232 --> 02:27:47,609
Altmann, Eduard.

2029
02:27:48,276 --> 02:27:49,823
Grunberg, Miriam.

2030
02:27:50,278 --> 02:27:51,905
Luftig, Eliasz.

2031
02:27:52,739 --> 02:27:53,991
Hilmann, Eduard.

2032
02:27:54,574 --> 02:27:55,951
Erna Rothberg.

2033
02:27:57,243 --> 02:27:58,495
Zuckermann, Jetti.

2034
02:28:00,330 --> 02:28:01,707
Helen Hirsch.

2035
02:28:02,582 --> 02:28:03,629
(PENCIL SCRAPING PAPER)

2036
02:28:04,125 --> 02:28:05,968
The worst is over.

2037
02:28:07,545 --> 02:28:10,515
Men to this transport and women to this transport.

2038
02:28:11,841 --> 02:28:12,742
Be careful.

2039
02:28:13,341 --> 02:28:16,442
Men to this transport and women to this transport.

2040
02:28:16,805 --> 02:28:20,776
Watch your step. Men to this transport
and women to this transport.

2041
02:28:39,494 --> 02:28:41,997
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

2042
02:28:42,831 --> 02:28:44,424
(PEOPLE COUGHING)

2043
02:28:59,264 --> 02:29:03,189
Wonderful, Olek, wonderful.

2044
02:29:03,685 --> 02:29:07,059
You know how we make ice into water?

2045
02:29:07,439 --> 02:29:09,441
(BLOWING)

2046
02:29:09,524 --> 02:29:11,067
Olek, get another one!

2047
02:29:20,452 --> 02:29:22,375
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

2048
02:29:35,717 --> 02:29:37,469
(PEOPLE COUGHING)

2049
02:29:49,814 --> 02:29:51,612
MAN: Alle in einer Einzelreihe aufstellen!

2050
02:29:53,485 --> 02:29:56,455
You'll be pleased with the level of efficiency
I get from these workers.

2051
02:29:59,657 --> 02:30:01,830
Budzyn, under my command,

2052
02:30:01,910 --> 02:30:04,914
was the envy of every other
commandant in the labor camp system.

2053
02:30:05,079 --> 02:30:06,376
- The prisoners, however...
- Excuse me.

2054
02:30:06,456 --> 02:30:08,125
They would have rather been somewhere else.

2055
02:30:23,681 --> 02:30:27,106
SCHINDLER: The train with the women has already left Plaszow

2056
02:30:27,393 --> 02:30:29,896
and will be arriving here very shortly.

2057
02:30:30,772 --> 02:30:33,275
I know you've had a long journey.

2058
02:30:33,691 --> 02:30:36,535
But it's only a short walk further to the factory,

2059
02:30:36,778 --> 02:30:40,453
where hot soup and bread is waiting for you.

2060
02:30:42,575 --> 02:30:44,093
Welcome to Brinnlitz!

2061
02:30:46,871 --> 02:30:48,965
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

2062
02:30:54,295 --> 02:30:55,717
MRS. DRESNER: Beans in cholent?

2063
02:30:55,838 --> 02:30:57,306
MILA: Beans are the best part.

2064
02:30:57,507 --> 02:30:58,929
DANKA: I don't like beans.

2065
02:30:59,968 --> 02:31:03,472
Beans and meat and potatoes and bread.

2066
02:31:03,846 --> 02:31:06,065
That's not the way you make cholent.

2067
02:31:10,478 --> 02:31:11,604
Eggs in cholent?

2068
02:31:11,729 --> 02:31:12,855
Yes!

2069
02:31:16,109 --> 02:31:17,235
DANKA: I don't like cholent.

2070
02:31:17,360 --> 02:31:18,486
MRS. DRESNER: No, you don't.

2071
02:31:18,903 --> 02:31:19,995
What do you like?

2072
02:31:20,113 --> 02:31:21,205
I like caviar.

2073
02:31:24,033 --> 02:31:25,660
REBEKA: One day on the fire...

2074
02:31:25,743 --> 02:31:27,586
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

2075
02:32:30,725 --> 02:32:32,648
(DOGS BARKING AND SNARLING)

2076
02:32:32,727 --> 02:32:34,775
Alle vorm Wagen in Position bleiben.

2077
02:32:36,346 --> 02:32:38,992
Alle in der Gruppe zusammenbleiben.

2078
02:32:39,484 --> 02:32:41,111
Wegbleiben vom Wagen!

2079
02:32:41,611 --> 02:32:43,739
Wegbleiben vom Wagen!

2080
02:32:44,030 --> 02:32:47,034
Wegbleiben vom Wagen, hab ich gesagt!

2081
02:32:51,912 --> 02:32:54,587
Schneller! Dalli, dalli, dalli!

2082
02:32:55,874 --> 02:32:57,718
Was ist da hinten los!

2083
02:32:58,544 --> 02:32:59,545
(DOG BARKING)

2084
02:33:00,721 --> 02:33:01,344
SOLDIER: Schnell!

2085
02:33:07,261 --> 02:33:09,355
SOLDIER: Los, raus mit euch. Zack, zack, zack! Raus!

2086
02:33:10,765 --> 02:33:13,614
Dreißig, fünfunddreißig,

2087
02:33:14,200 --> 02:33:15,326
vierzig,

2088
02:33:16,243 --> 02:33:17,653
fünfundvierzig.

2089
02:33:18,606 --> 02:33:20,950
SOLDIER: Aussteigen!

2090
02:33:32,203 --> 02:33:33,855
Where are the list makers?

2091
02:33:33,921 --> 02:33:35,018
Where are the tables?

2092
02:33:40,795 --> 02:33:42,342
Raus mit euch!

2093
02:33:43,631 --> 02:33:44,632
Hopp, hopp!

2094
02:33:44,716 --> 02:33:46,810
...bagaze w wagonach!

2095
02:33:47,719 --> 02:33:50,472
Dalli! Rausgehen! Schneller!

2096
02:33:50,930 --> 02:33:53,353
Zostawcie bagaze w wagonach!

2097
02:33:54,058 --> 02:33:55,401
Schneller!

2098
02:33:55,476 --> 02:33:57,729
Los, ein bisschen schneller!

2099
02:33:58,104 --> 02:33:59,856
Mama, where are we?

2100
02:34:03,985 --> 02:34:05,278
They're in Auschwitz.

2101
02:34:05,653 --> 02:34:08,327
The train was never routed here. A paperwork mistake.

2102
02:34:15,872 --> 02:34:17,590
POLISH WOMAN: Szybciej! Szybko!

2103
02:34:17,665 --> 02:34:19,542
GERMAN WOMAN: Die Schuhe werfen!

2104
02:34:33,097 --> 02:34:35,691
- Schneller! Schneller!
- Ubrania skladac!

2105
02:34:38,478 --> 02:34:41,027
- Pod prysznic!
- Zieht euch aus! Bewegung!

2106
02:34:41,105 --> 02:34:43,824
Bewegt euch! Stellt euch auf und zieht euch aus!

2107
02:34:43,900 --> 02:34:47,029
- Rozbierac sie tam szybciej!
- Schneller!

2108
02:34:48,571 --> 02:34:50,699
WOMAN: Szybko sie rozbierac.

2109
02:34:51,532 --> 02:34:55,787
Dostaniecie mydlo i recznik i
pojdziecie pod prysznic do dezynfeckji!

2110
02:34:55,870 --> 02:34:57,213
Szybko sie rozbierac!

2111
02:35:01,834 --> 02:35:04,804
- Schneller!
- Zabierajcie to mydlo i szybko!

2112
02:35:04,879 --> 02:35:07,723
- Zieht euch schneller aus!
- Bewegung!

2113
02:35:14,388 --> 02:35:17,107
- Szybko! Szybko!
- Sofort hinein! Schneller!

2114
02:35:17,767 --> 02:35:19,815
Pojdziecie pod prysznic! Szybko!

2115
02:35:19,894 --> 02:35:21,271
Schneller!

2116
02:35:21,896 --> 02:35:23,990
Hinein zum Bad! Schneller!

2117
02:35:26,734 --> 02:35:29,738
Schneller! Schneller!

2118
02:35:31,572 --> 02:35:33,324
Szybko! Szybko!

2119
02:35:34,033 --> 02:35:35,250
Tu wchodzic!

2120
02:35:53,761 --> 02:35:56,184
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

2121
02:36:00,768 --> 02:36:02,441
(SOBBING)

2122
02:36:08,276 --> 02:36:09,573
(SOBBING)

2123
02:36:10,695 --> 02:36:12,948
(WOMEN WAILING)

2124
02:36:29,714 --> 02:36:31,591
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

2125
02:36:36,137 --> 02:36:37,514
(EXCLAIMS IN SURPRISE)

2126
02:36:55,656 --> 02:36:57,203
(LAUGHING)

2127
02:38:01,055 --> 02:38:02,272
Blick hinunter!

2128
02:38:05,726 --> 02:38:07,728
Die Hand auf die Schulter!

2129
02:38:08,646 --> 02:38:09,898
MAN: How old are you, mother?

2130
02:38:10,064 --> 02:38:11,361
WOMAN: Sixty-eight.

2131
02:38:11,565 --> 02:38:12,657
Cough for me, mother.

2132
02:38:12,817 --> 02:38:16,572
They say to fall against the fence is a kindness.

2133
02:38:16,988 --> 02:38:20,037
Don't kill yourself against the fence, Clara.

2134
02:38:20,116 --> 02:38:22,869
If you do, you'll never know what happened to you.

2135
02:38:25,955 --> 02:38:27,207
How old are you, mother?

2136
02:38:27,331 --> 02:38:28,583
Sixty-six, sir.

2137
02:38:28,666 --> 02:38:30,714
- Sir?
- Good morning.

2138
02:38:30,793 --> 02:38:33,797
A mistake has been made.
We are not supposed to be here.

2139
02:38:33,879 --> 02:38:37,304
We work for Oskar Schindler. We are Schindler Jews.

2140
02:38:37,758 --> 02:38:39,431
Who is Oskar Schindler?

2141
02:38:39,552 --> 02:38:41,179
He had a factory in Krakow.

2142
02:38:41,262 --> 02:38:42,639
Enamelware.

2143
02:38:43,472 --> 02:38:45,065
A pot maker.

2144
02:38:46,100 --> 02:38:47,818
How old are you, mother?

2145
02:38:52,648 --> 02:38:56,023
You are not the only industrialist who needs labor,

2146
02:38:58,279 --> 02:38:59,451
Herr Schindler.

2147
02:39:00,948 --> 02:39:03,622
I remember earlier this year, IG Farben ordered

2148
02:39:03,701 --> 02:39:07,956
a trainload of Hungarians for its chemical factory.

2149
02:39:09,749 --> 02:39:12,468
The train came in through the archway

2150
02:39:13,669 --> 02:39:17,515
and the officer in charge of the
selection went immediately to work

2151
02:39:19,467 --> 02:39:21,310
and sent 2,000 of them

2152
02:39:22,094 --> 02:39:24,267
straight away to Special Treatment.

2153
02:39:26,474 --> 02:39:28,647
It is not my task to interfere with

2154
02:39:28,809 --> 02:39:31,028
the processes that take place down here.

2155
02:39:33,147 --> 02:39:38,125
Why do you think I can help you if I can't help IG Farben?

2156
02:39:38,319 --> 02:39:40,196
Allow me to express the reason.

2157
02:39:50,247 --> 02:39:52,750
I'm not making any judgment about you.

2158
02:39:53,542 --> 02:39:56,295
It's just that I know that in the coming months,

2159
02:39:56,378 --> 02:39:59,052
we're all going to need portable wealth.

2160
02:40:02,718 --> 02:40:04,812
I could have you arrested.

2161
02:40:05,471 --> 02:40:09,271
I'm protected by powerful friends. You should know that.

2162
02:40:13,270 --> 02:40:15,739
I do not say I am accepting them.

2163
02:40:17,316 --> 02:40:20,445
All I say is, I'm not comfortable with them on the table.

2164
02:40:36,085 --> 02:40:38,338
I have a shipment coming in tomorrow.

2165
02:40:39,380 --> 02:40:41,303
I'll cut you 300 units from it.

2166
02:40:41,715 --> 02:40:44,889
New ones. These are fresh.

2167
02:40:49,523 --> 02:40:53,394
- The train comes, we turn it around.
- Mmm, yes, yes.

2168
02:40:53,477 --> 02:40:55,150
- It's yours.
- I understand.

2169
02:40:55,563 --> 02:40:57,031
I want these.

2170
02:41:01,026 --> 02:41:03,120
You shouldn't get stuck on names.

2171
02:41:11,162 --> 02:41:14,382
That's right. It creates a lot of paperwork.

2172
02:41:15,541 --> 02:41:19,466
Zoldinger, Ernestina! Waldergrun, Hilda!

2173
02:41:19,670 --> 02:41:21,513
Waldergrun, Leonora!

2174
02:41:21,797 --> 02:41:25,301
Laast, Anna! Pfefferberg, Mila!

2175
02:41:25,426 --> 02:41:28,930
Dresner, Chaja! Dresner, Danka!

2176
02:41:29,054 --> 02:41:32,433
Nussbaum, Sidonia! Rosner, Manci!

2177
02:41:32,766 --> 02:41:38,023
Hirsch, Helen! Grosz, Chaja Sara! Seelenfreund, Estella!

2178
02:41:38,105 --> 02:41:39,106
(DOGS BARKING)

2179
02:41:39,190 --> 02:41:40,612
(WOMEN SHOUTING)

2180
02:41:53,537 --> 02:41:56,916
WOMAN SOLDIER: Schneller laufen! Schneller laufen! Schneller!

2181
02:41:57,166 --> 02:41:59,635
- Schneller! Schneller!
- Mach schon! Voran!

2182
02:42:01,045 --> 02:42:04,094
Los, los, los! Schneller!

2183
02:42:07,134 --> 02:42:10,308
SOLDIERS: Schneller! Bewegt euch!

2184
02:42:11,597 --> 02:42:13,395
Bojcie sie! Bojcie sie!

2185
02:42:17,978 --> 02:42:18,979
(SCREAMING)

2186
02:42:19,104 --> 02:42:20,981
No! No! No!

2187
02:42:24,652 --> 02:42:28,498
WOMAN SOLDIER: Mädchen, los jetzt aber! Jetzt aber Tempo!

2188
02:42:31,700 --> 02:42:33,373
(SCREAMING)

2189
02:42:35,788 --> 02:42:38,291
(SHRIEKING)

2190
02:42:40,334 --> 02:42:43,929
Danka! Danka! Danka!

2191
02:42:44,004 --> 02:42:46,427
No! No! No!

2192
02:42:46,507 --> 02:42:48,805
(SCREAMING)

2193
02:42:48,884 --> 02:42:52,354
Hey! Hey! Hey! What are you doing?

2194
02:42:52,763 --> 02:42:56,518
These are mine! These are my workers!
They should be on my train!

2195
02:42:57,518 --> 02:42:59,816
They're skilled munitions workers! They're essential!

2196
02:43:00,688 --> 02:43:02,235
Essential girls!

2197
02:43:03,357 --> 02:43:04,358
(SHRIEKS)

2198
02:43:05,609 --> 02:43:09,409
Their fingers polish the insides of shell metal casings.

2199
02:43:10,030 --> 02:43:11,703
How else am I to polish the inside

2200
02:43:11,865 --> 02:43:13,538
of a 45 millimeter shell casing?

2201
02:43:13,701 --> 02:43:15,829
You tell me. You tell me!

2202
02:43:18,789 --> 02:43:22,214
Back on the train! Back on the train!

2203
02:43:24,586 --> 02:43:27,556
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

2204
02:45:17,408 --> 02:45:20,378
Under Department "W" provisions

2205
02:45:21,537 --> 02:45:24,461
it is unlawful to kill a worker without just cause.

2206
02:45:26,041 --> 02:45:28,544
Under the Businesses Compensation Fund

2207
02:45:29,169 --> 02:45:32,013
I am entitled to file damage claims for such deaths.

2208
02:45:33,424 --> 02:45:35,677
If you shoot without thinking,

2209
02:45:36,635 --> 02:45:39,855
you go to prison, I get paid.

2210
02:45:41,014 --> 02:45:42,361
That's how it works.

2211
02:45:43,308 --> 02:45:47,029
So, there will be no summary executions here.

2212
02:45:49,356 --> 02:45:52,530
There will be no interference of any kind with production.

2213
02:45:54,194 --> 02:45:55,892
In hopes of ensuring that,

2214
02:45:56,013 --> 02:45:58,866
guards will no longer be allowed on the factory floor

2215
02:45:59,366 --> 02:46:01,664
without my authorization.

2216
02:46:07,791 --> 02:46:10,635
For your cooperation, you have my gratitude.

2217
02:46:12,713 --> 02:46:14,431
Come on, come.

2218
02:46:15,549 --> 02:46:17,768
SOLDIER: Mensch, seit Jahren hab ich so etwas nicht mehr gesehen.

2219
02:46:17,885 --> 02:46:21,389
- SCHINDLER: Come on, boys, come.
- Guck dir mal die Buddeln an!

2220
02:46:21,763 --> 02:46:26,519
PRIEST: Et dimitte nobis debita nostra...

2221
02:46:26,602 --> 02:46:30,323
sicut et nos dimittimus...

2222
02:46:30,397 --> 02:46:35,449
CONGREGATION: ...quotidianum da nobis hodie.

2223
02:46:35,527 --> 02:46:39,907
Et dimitte nobis debita nostra...

2224
02:46:40,282 --> 02:46:43,502
sicut et nos dimittimus...

2225
02:46:43,577 --> 02:46:46,751
debitoribus nostris...

2226
02:46:46,830 --> 02:46:51,210
No doorman or maître d'will ever mistake you again.

2227
02:46:52,836 --> 02:46:54,008
I promise.

2228
02:46:54,087 --> 02:46:56,931
...sed libera nos a malo

2229
02:46:58,992 --> 02:46:59,514
Itzhak.

2230
02:47:01,929 --> 02:47:03,730
This is Itzhak Stern, my accountant. Itzhak...

2231
02:47:03,764 --> 02:47:05,437
You must be Mrs. Schindler.

2232
02:47:05,599 --> 02:47:06,717
It's a pleasure to meet you.

2233
02:47:06,717 --> 02:47:08,314
Emilie has volunteered to work in the clinic.

2234
02:47:08,435 --> 02:47:10,153
- Very generous of you.
- I know.

2235
02:47:10,229 --> 02:47:11,607
We need to talk when you have a moment.

2236
02:47:13,148 --> 02:47:15,526
This is my wife, Stern.
I don't keep any secrets from my spouse.

2237
02:47:15,609 --> 02:47:18,362
Oskar, please, attend to business.
It's much more attractive.

2238
02:47:18,737 --> 02:47:19,829
- Madam.
- Hello.

2239
02:47:19,905 --> 02:47:21,665
- What is it?
- We've received an angry complaint

2240
02:47:21,740 --> 02:47:23,058
from the Armaments Board.

2241
02:47:23,534 --> 02:47:25,662
The artillery shells, tank shells, rocket casings,

2242
02:47:25,744 --> 02:47:28,293
apparently all of them have failed quality control tests.

2243
02:47:28,413 --> 02:47:30,461
That's to be expected. Start-up problems.

2244
02:47:30,541 --> 02:47:32,714
This isn't pots and pans. This is a precise business.

2245
02:47:32,834 --> 02:47:34,677
- I'll write them a letter.
- They're withholding payment.

2246
02:47:34,753 --> 02:47:36,596
Sure, so would I, so would you.

2247
02:47:36,672 --> 02:47:39,016
I wouldn't worry about it.
We'll get it right one of these days.

2248
02:47:39,091 --> 02:47:42,391
There's a rumor you've been going
around miscalibrating the machines.

2249
02:47:43,720 --> 02:47:46,644
They could shut us down, send us back to Auschwitz.

2250
02:47:49,476 --> 02:47:51,649
I'll call around, find out where we can buy shells.

2251
02:47:51,728 --> 02:47:52,529
Pass them off as ours.

2252
02:47:52,554 --> 02:47:53,935
I don't see the difference.

2253
02:47:53,981 --> 02:47:55,073
Whether they're made here or somewhere else...

2254
02:47:55,148 --> 02:47:56,741
You don't see a difference? I see a difference.

2255
02:47:56,817 --> 02:47:57,784
You'll lose a lot of money.

2256
02:47:57,859 --> 02:47:59,257
Fewer shells will be made.

2257
02:47:59,736 --> 02:48:01,534
Stern, if this factory ever produces

2258
02:48:01,655 --> 02:48:03,498
a shell that can actually be fired,

2259
02:48:03,574 --> 02:48:05,042
I'll be very unhappy.

2260
02:48:06,910 --> 02:48:08,958
- WOMAN: Hello, madam.
- How do you do?

2261
02:48:19,923 --> 02:48:21,175
(MACHINE GRINDING)

2262
02:48:23,294 --> 02:48:24,473
How are you doing, Rabbi?

2263
02:48:25,778 --> 02:48:26,529
Rabbi!

2264
02:48:30,142 --> 02:48:31,219
Good, Herr Direktor.

2265
02:48:33,879 --> 02:48:35,047
Sun's going down.

2266
02:48:38,525 --> 02:48:39,993
Yes, it is.

2267
02:48:41,862 --> 02:48:43,883
What day is this? Friday?

2268
02:48:44,296 --> 02:48:45,556
It is Friday, isn't it?

2269
02:48:45,782 --> 02:48:46,674
Is it?

2270
02:48:51,455 --> 02:48:55,176
What's the matter with you?
You should be preparing for the Sabbath.

2271
02:48:56,376 --> 02:48:57,753
Shouldn't you?

2272
02:49:05,427 --> 02:49:09,227
I've got some wine. In my office. Come.

2273
02:49:13,477 --> 02:49:17,198
RABBI LETARTOV: Savree maranun verabonun verobotay

2274
02:49:19,191 --> 02:49:26,040
Baruch atah, Adoshem eloheynu, melech ha-olam

2275
02:49:26,365 --> 02:49:30,211
Boray p'ree ha-gafen

2276
02:49:30,619 --> 02:49:31,916
WORKERS: Amen.

2277
02:49:32,954 --> 02:49:36,208
Baruch atah, Adoshem eloheynu, melech ha-olam

2278
02:49:36,291 --> 02:49:39,340
A-sher kid'shanu b'mitzvo-tav v'ratza va-nu

2279
02:49:39,419 --> 02:49:44,971
V'shabbat kaddsho b'ahavah oov-ratzone hin-cheelanu

2280
02:49:45,717 --> 02:49:48,186
Zeekaron Pma-ahsay v'raysheet

2281
02:49:48,261 --> 02:49:53,518
Kee hoo yom t'cheelah Pmikraay
kodesh zaycher leetzeeat mitzrayim

2282
02:49:53,600 --> 02:50:00,199
Kee vanu vachatah v'ohtahnu
keydashta mekol ha-ahmim

2283
02:50:00,273 --> 02:50:05,575
V'shabbat kadd-shcha b'ahavah
oov-ratzone hin-chal-ta-nu

2284
02:50:05,654 --> 02:50:10,875
Baruch atah, Adoshem, m'kaddaysh ha-Shabbat

2285
02:50:12,953 --> 02:50:14,045
Gut Shabbos.

2286
02:50:14,121 --> 02:50:15,374
(WORKERS RESPOND) Gut Shabbos.

2287
02:50:25,006 --> 02:50:26,349
SCHINDLER: What?

2288
02:50:28,218 --> 02:50:33,224
Do you have any money hidden away someplace

2289
02:50:33,306 --> 02:50:34,599
that I don't know about?

2290
02:50:39,354 --> 02:50:40,246
No.

2291
02:50:46,278 --> 02:50:47,905
Why? Am I broke?

2292
02:50:50,031 --> 02:50:51,032
Uh...

2293
02:50:53,201 --> 02:50:54,498
Well...

2294
02:50:56,496 --> 02:51:01,502
WINSTON CHURCHILL ON RADIO: Yesterday morning, at 2:41 a.m.,

2295
02:51:02,836 --> 02:51:05,760
at General Eisenhower's headquarters,

2296
02:51:06,840 --> 02:51:12,847
General Jodl signed the Act of Unconditional Surrender

2297
02:51:14,055 --> 02:51:18,936
of all German land, sea and air forces in Europe

2298
02:51:19,978 --> 02:51:22,527
to the Allied Expeditionary Force

2299
02:51:23,857 --> 02:51:27,953
and simultaneously to the Soviet High Command.

2300
02:51:28,737 --> 02:51:31,331
The German war is, therefore, at an end.

2301
02:51:31,406 --> 02:51:32,532
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

2302
02:51:32,657 --> 02:51:34,625
(KNOCKING AT DOOR) But let us not forget for a moment...

2303
02:51:34,701 --> 02:51:37,750
I think it's time the guards came into the factory.

2304
02:51:39,372 --> 02:51:41,215
Japan, with all her treachery...

2305
02:51:42,375 --> 02:51:46,221
The unconditional surrender of
Germany has just been announced.

2306
02:51:48,048 --> 02:51:51,848
At midnight tonight, the war is over.

2307
02:51:54,721 --> 02:51:56,974
Tomorrow you'll begin the process

2308
02:51:57,098 --> 02:51:59,396
of looking for survivors of your families.

2309
02:52:03,230 --> 02:52:04,698
In most cases,

2310
02:52:06,733 --> 02:52:08,576
you won't find them.

2311
02:52:09,903 --> 02:52:12,122
After six long years of murder,

2312
02:52:12,823 --> 02:52:15,793
victims are being mourned throughout the world.

2313
02:52:18,245 --> 02:52:19,492
We've survived.

2314
02:52:21,540 --> 02:52:24,089
Many of you have come up to me and thanked me.

2315
02:52:27,712 --> 02:52:29,385
Thank yourselves.

2316
02:52:31,258 --> 02:52:33,306
Thank your fearless Stern

2317
02:52:34,469 --> 02:52:36,437
and others among you who worried about you

2318
02:52:36,555 --> 02:52:38,433
and faced death at every moment.

2319
02:52:43,645 --> 02:52:45,489
I'm a member of the Nazi Party.

2320
02:52:46,648 --> 02:52:48,401
I'm a munitions manufacturer.

2321
02:52:49,693 --> 02:52:51,287
I'm a profiteer of slave labor.

2322
02:52:52,445 --> 02:52:54,368
I am a criminal.

2323
02:52:56,324 --> 02:52:59,053
At midnight you'll be free, and I'll be hunted.

2324
02:53:01,872 --> 02:53:04,876
I shall remain with you until five minutes after midnight,

2325
02:53:05,458 --> 02:53:08,632
after which time, and I hope you'll forgive me,

2326
02:53:08,712 --> 02:53:10,259
I have to flee.

2327
02:53:13,717 --> 02:53:16,371
I know you have received orders from our commandant,

2328
02:53:17,512 --> 02:53:19,340
which he has received from his superiors,

2329
02:53:19,406 --> 02:53:21,934
to dispose of the population of this camp.

2330
02:53:23,018 --> 02:53:25,037
Now would be the time to do it.

2331
02:53:25,312 --> 02:53:27,043
Here they are, they're all here.

2332
02:53:28,539 --> 02:53:29,943
This is your opportunity.

2333
02:53:30,025 --> 02:53:31,993
(PEOPLE MURMURING)

2334
02:53:35,155 --> 02:53:36,828
Or you could leave

2335
02:53:39,075 --> 02:53:41,044
and return to your families as men

2336
02:53:41,620 --> 02:53:43,063
instead of murderers.

2337
02:54:25,872 --> 02:54:28,576
In memory of the countless victims among your people,

2338
02:54:29,709 --> 02:54:32,713
I ask us to observe three minutes of silence.

2339
02:54:40,462 --> 02:54:45,438
RABBI LEVARTOV: Yitgadal veyitkadash shemey raba

2340
02:54:45,892 --> 02:54:49,817
Be'olma di'vera chir'utey veyamlich malchutey

2341
02:54:49,896 --> 02:54:53,867
Ve'yatzmach purkaney vi'ykarev meshichey

2342
02:54:53,942 --> 02:54:59,073
Bechayeychon u'veyomeychon
u'vechayey di chol beyt yisrael

2343
02:54:59,155 --> 02:55:02,705
Ba'agala u'vizman kariv ve'imru amen

2344
02:55:02,784 --> 02:55:03,910
WORKERS: Amen.

2345
02:55:04,285 --> 02:55:08,586
Yehey sh'mey raba mevorach le'olam u'le'olmey olmaya

2346
02:55:08,665 --> 02:55:12,852
Yitbarach ve'yishtabach ve'yitpa'ar
ve'yitromam ve'yitnasey

2347
02:55:12,852 --> 02:55:15,505
Ve'yithadar ve'yit'aleh ve'yiythalal

2348
02:55:15,588 --> 02:55:18,307
She'mey dikudsha b'rich hu

2349
02:55:19,259 --> 02:55:23,264
Yehey sh'lama raba min shemaya ve'chayim tovim

2350
02:55:23,346 --> 02:55:27,146
Aleynu ve'al kol yisrael ve'imru amen

2351
02:55:27,225 --> 02:55:28,272
WORKERS: Amen.

2352
02:55:28,810 --> 02:55:31,438
- Thank you, Mr. Jereth.
- Thank you, Mr. Jereth.

2353
02:55:32,022 --> 02:55:34,266
- Thank you, Mr. Jereth.
- Thank you, Mr. Jereth.

2354
02:55:34,324 --> 02:55:35,316
STERN: Open wide.

2355
02:55:38,111 --> 02:55:39,313
Thank you, Mr. Jereth.

2356
02:55:58,631 --> 02:56:00,029
Thank you, Mr. Jereth.

2357
02:56:25,492 --> 02:56:28,211
As soon as peace occurs, I want...

2358
02:56:29,913 --> 02:56:32,632
I want that cloth distributed to the workers.

2359
02:56:33,666 --> 02:56:35,794
Two and a half meters each.

2360
02:56:36,419 --> 02:56:39,093
Also, each person is to get a bottle of vodka.

2361
02:56:39,798 --> 02:56:41,971
They won't drink it. They know its value.

2362
02:56:42,717 --> 02:56:45,846
Likewise those Egipshi cigarettes we organized.

2363
02:56:46,346 --> 02:56:48,849
It'll be done. Everything you ask.

2364
02:57:09,702 --> 02:57:12,972
We've written a letter, trying to explain things

2365
02:57:14,207 --> 02:57:15,679
in case you are captured.

2366
02:57:18,461 --> 02:57:20,189
Every worker has signed it.

2367
02:57:31,724 --> 02:57:32,746
Thank you.

2368
02:58:00,795 --> 02:58:02,797
It is Hebrew, from the Talmud.

2369
02:58:02,881 --> 02:58:06,385
It says, "Whoever saves one life, saves the world entire."

2370
02:58:14,267 --> 02:58:15,644
(RING CLATTERING)

2371
02:58:47,634 --> 02:58:49,557
I could have got more out.

2372
02:58:52,639 --> 02:58:54,812
I could have got more. I don't know.

2373
02:58:55,141 --> 02:58:56,393
If I just...

2374
02:58:58,645 --> 02:58:59,692
I could have got more.

2375
02:58:59,771 --> 02:59:03,072
Oskar, there are 1,100 people who are alive because of you.

2376
02:59:03,074 --> 02:59:04,072
Look at them.

2377
02:59:05,693 --> 02:59:07,661
If I'd made more money.

2378
02:59:08,238 --> 02:59:09,455
(LAUGHS)

2379
02:59:11,991 --> 02:59:15,211
I threw away so much money.

2380
02:59:17,872 --> 02:59:20,466
(SOBBING) You have no idea.

2381
02:59:21,876 --> 02:59:23,219
If I had just...

2382
02:59:23,294 --> 02:59:26,173
There will be generations because of what you did.

2383
02:59:28,508 --> 02:59:30,260
I didn't do enough.

2384
02:59:31,177 --> 02:59:32,770
You did so much.

2385
02:59:37,141 --> 02:59:38,438
This car.

2386
02:59:39,894 --> 02:59:42,022
Goeth would've bought this car.

2387
02:59:42,105 --> 02:59:45,609
Why did I keep the car? Ten people right there.

2388
02:59:49,404 --> 02:59:50,997
Ten people.

2389
02:59:53,032 --> 02:59:54,659
Ten more people.

2390
02:59:57,453 --> 02:59:59,046
This pin...

2391
02:59:59,163 --> 03:00:00,585
Two people.

2392
03:00:03,668 --> 03:00:05,136
This is gold.

2393
03:00:05,670 --> 03:00:07,263
Two more people.

2394
03:00:07,547 --> 03:00:10,551
He would have given me two for it, at least one.

2395
03:00:10,675 --> 03:00:12,723
He would have given me one, one more.

2396
03:00:16,180 --> 03:00:17,807
One more person.

2397
03:00:20,435 --> 03:00:22,062
A person, Stern.

2398
03:00:24,355 --> 03:00:25,698
For this.

2399
03:00:28,401 --> 03:00:31,450
(SOBBING) I could have gotten

2400
03:00:32,196 --> 03:00:35,666
one more person, and I didn't.

2401
03:00:37,243 --> 03:00:38,961
And I didn't!

2402
03:00:39,162 --> 03:00:40,914
(LOUD SOBBING)

2403
03:02:09,585 --> 03:02:11,804
You have been liberated

2404
03:02:12,255 --> 03:02:14,257
